            {
              "id": "CWE-476",
              "name": "CVE-2026-8723 in qs 6.14.2 via express (TypeError DoS in stringify with comma arrayFormat)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8723 in qs 6.14.2 via express (TypeError DoS in stringify with comma arrayFormat)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The transitive package **`qs@6.14.2`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `express`) is affected by CVE-2026-8723: `qs.stringify` throws a synchronous `TypeError` when called with `arrayFormat: 'comma'` and `encodeValuesOnly: true` on an array containing `null`/`undefined` — the comma + encodeValuesOnly branch maps through a raw encode of the null value. Not guarded by `skipNulls`/`strictNullHandling`. Causes an uncaught exception / process-level DoS when this code path is hit. Fixed in `6.15.2`."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The transitive package **`qs@6.14.2`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `express`) is affected by CVE-2026-8723: `qs.stringify` throws a synchronous `TypeError` when called with `arrayFormat: 'comma'` and `encodeValuesOnly: true` on an array containing `null`/`undefined` — the comma + encodeValuesOnly branch maps through a raw encode of the null value. Not guarded by `skipNulls`/`strictNullHandling`. Causes an uncaught exception / process-level DoS when this code path is hit. Fixed in `6.15.2`.\n\nUncaught `TypeError` from `qs.stringify(null, {arrayFormat:'comma', encodeValuesOnly:true})` can crash the request handler (low availability impact) when the app stringifies arrays that may contain null/undefined.\n\nBump `express` to a release whose `qs` dependency floor is `>=6.15.2`, or `pnpm.overrides: { \"qs@<6.15.2\": \"^6.15.2\" }`. Regenerate lockfile, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`.",
                "markdown": "The transitive package **`qs@6.14.2`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `express`) is affected by CVE-2026-8723: `qs.stringify` throws a synchronous `TypeError` when called with `arrayFormat: 'comma'` and `encodeValuesOnly: true` on an array containing `null`/`undefined` — the comma + encodeValuesOnly branch maps through a raw encode of the null value. Not guarded by `skipNulls`/`strictNullHandling`. Causes an uncaught exception / process-level DoS when this code path is hit. Fixed in `6.15.2`.\n\nUncaught `TypeError` from `qs.stringify(null, {arrayFormat:'comma', encodeValuesOnly:true})` can crash the request handler (low availability impact) when the app stringifies arrays that may contain null/undefined.\n\nBump `express` to a release whose `qs` dependency floor is `>=6.15.2`, or `pnpm.overrides: { \"qs@<6.15.2\": \"^6.15.2\" }`. Regenerate lockfile, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-476",
                  "CVE-2026-8723",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html"
