            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-14257",
              "name": "CVE-2026-14257 in brace-expansion 1.1.12 / 2.1.0 (memory-exhaustion DoS in expand())",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-14257 in brace-expansion 1.1.12 / 2.1.0 (memory-exhaustion DoS in expand())"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Two pinned copies of **`brace-expansion`** (`1.1.12` and `2.1.0`) are affected by CVE-2026-14257: memory exhaustion in the `expand()` function on crafted patterns. Fixed in `1.1.17` / `2.1.3` / `3.0.3` / `5.0.8`. Reached via `minimatch` under `glob`, through `duckdb`'s build chain."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Two pinned copies of **`brace-expansion`** (`1.1.12` and `2.1.0`) are affected by CVE-2026-14257: memory exhaustion in the `expand()` function on crafted patterns. Fixed in `1.1.17` / `2.1.3` / `3.0.3` / `5.0.8`. Reached via `minimatch` under `glob`, through `duckdb`'s build chain.\n\nMemory exhaustion in `expand()` on adversarial brace patterns, in the duckdb native build/fetch toolchain path. Availability impact.\n\n`pnpm.overrides` for both majors: `\"brace-expansion@<1.1.18\": \"^1.1.18\"` and `\"brace-expansion@>=2.0.0 <2.1.4\": \"^2.1.4\"` (covers all four brace-expansion CVEs), then `pnpm install` and verify.",
                "markdown": "Two pinned copies of **`brace-expansion`** (`1.1.12` and `2.1.0`) are affected by CVE-2026-14257: memory exhaustion in the `expand()` function on crafted patterns. Fixed in `1.1.17` / `2.1.3` / `3.0.3` / `5.0.8`. Reached via `minimatch` under `glob`, through `duckdb`'s build chain.\n\nMemory exhaustion in `expand()` on adversarial brace patterns, in the duckdb native build/fetch toolchain path. Availability impact.\n\n`pnpm.overrides` for both majors: `\"brace-expansion@<1.1.18\": \"^1.1.18\"` and `\"brace-expansion@>=2.0.0 <2.1.4\": \"^2.1.4\"` (covers all four brace-expansion CVEs), then `pnpm install` and verify."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CVE-2026-14257",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-69152",
              "name": "CVE-2026-69152 in brace-expansion 1.1.12 / 2.1.0 (DoS via unbounded intermediate arrays — bypass of CVE-2026-14257 mitigation)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-69152 in brace-expansion 1.1.12 / 2.1.0 (DoS via unbounded intermediate arrays — bypass of CVE-2026-14257 mitigation)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Two pinned copies of **`brace-expansion`** (`1.1.12` and `2.1.0`) are affected by CVE-2026-69152: unbounded intermediate arrays cause DoS, bypassing the earlier CVE-2026-14257 mitigation. Fixed in `1.1.18` / `2.1.4` / `3.0.6` / `5.0.9`."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Two pinned copies of **`brace-expansion`** (`1.1.12` and `2.1.0`) are affected by CVE-2026-69152: unbounded intermediate arrays cause DoS, bypassing the earlier CVE-2026-14257 mitigation. Fixed in `1.1.18` / `2.1.4` / `3.0.6` / `5.0.9`.\n\nUnbounded intermediate arrays cause memory/CPU DoS in `expand()`, in the duckdb build toolchain path. Availability impact.\n\n`pnpm.overrides`: `\"brace-expansion@<1.1.18\": \"^1.1.18\"` and `\"brace-expansion@>=2.0.0 <2.1.4\": \"^2.1.4\"`, `pnpm install`, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`.",
                "markdown": "Two pinned copies of **`brace-expansion`** (`1.1.12` and `2.1.0`) are affected by CVE-2026-69152: unbounded intermediate arrays cause DoS, bypassing the earlier CVE-2026-14257 mitigation. Fixed in `1.1.18` / `2.1.4` / `3.0.6` / `5.0.9`.\n\nUnbounded intermediate arrays cause memory/CPU DoS in `expand()`, in the duckdb build toolchain path. Availability impact.\n\n`pnpm.overrides`: `\"brace-expansion@<1.1.18\": \"^1.1.18\"` and `\"brace-expansion@>=2.0.0 <2.1.4\": \"^2.1.4\"`, `pnpm install`, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`."
