            {
              "id": "CWE-489",
              "name": "Pre-auth test-auth bypass grants attacker-controlled tellus-superadmin via X-Tellus-Test-Auth header (globalAuth)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Pre-auth test-auth bypass grants attacker-controlled tellus-superadmin via X-Tellus-Test-Auth header (globalAuth)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The global authentication gate honors the `X-Tellus-Test-Auth` header and `Authorization: Bearer test-auth:...` whenever `NODE_ENV !== 'production'` and `TELLUS_TEST_HOOKS=1`, with **no source-address restriction**. The role list embedded in the header is copied verbatim into the fabricated principal, so an unauthenticated remote caller can assert `tellus-superadmin` (and `marking:TOP_SECRET`, `ontology-admin`) on every request. This yields full unauthenticated administrative access to the API."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The global authentication gate honors the `X-Tellus-Test-Auth` header and `Authorization: Bearer test-auth:...` whenever `NODE_ENV !== 'production'` and `TELLUS_TEST_HOOKS=1`, with **no source-address restriction**. The role list embedded in the header is copied verbatim into the fabricated principal, so an unauthenticated remote caller can assert `tellus-superadmin` (and `marking:TOP_SECRET`, `ontology-admin`) on every request. This yields full unauthenticated administrative access to the API.\n\nAny remote unauthenticated attacker becomes `tellus-superadmin` (and `marking:TOP_SECRET`), bypassing all Keycloak authentication and role authorization on every route protected by globalAuth. Demonstrated: `X-Tellus-Test-Auth: <uuid>:tellus-superadmin,ontology-admin,marking:TOP_SECRET` returns HTTP 200 with object-type data, and the same header gains access to superadmin-only grant management. Full confidentiality and integrity loss of the ontology.\n\n1. Never honor test-principal headers on network-reachable deployments. Move the entire test-auth bypass out of `globalAuth`’s request path and behind an explicit, source-address-and-environment guard.\n2. Require BOTH `NODE_ENV` to be a non-production value **and** a distinct, rotation-capable shared secret (e.g. `TELLUS_TEST_HOOKS_SECRET`) that must accompany any test-auth assertion — never the flag alone.\n3. Add a source-address check (loopback only) mirroring `isLocalhost()` in `principal.ts` to both bypass branches in `globalAuth`; do not allow the header path to be more permissive than the code-repos fallback.\n4. Stop copying request-supplied roles verbatim; the principal builder should only accept a fixed allowlist of test users from `TEST_USER_SEEDS`, not arbitrary `userId`/role strings.\n5. Add a boot-time assertion that fails startup when `TELLUS_TEST_HOOKS=1` and the server is bound to a non-loopback interface, independent of `NODE_ENV`.",
                "markdown": "The global authentication gate honors the `X-Tellus-Test-Auth` header and `Authorization: Bearer test-auth:...` whenever `NODE_ENV !== 'production'` and `TELLUS_TEST_HOOKS=1`, with **no source-address restriction**. The role list embedded in the header is copied verbatim into the fabricated principal, so an unauthenticated remote caller can assert `tellus-superadmin` (and `marking:TOP_SECRET`, `ontology-admin`) on every request. This yields full unauthenticated administrative access to the API.\n\nAny remote unauthenticated attacker becomes `tellus-superadmin` (and `marking:TOP_SECRET`), bypassing all Keycloak authentication and role authorization on every route protected by globalAuth. Demonstrated: `X-Tellus-Test-Auth: <uuid>:tellus-superadmin,ontology-admin,marking:TOP_SECRET` returns HTTP 200 with object-type data, and the same header gains access to superadmin-only grant management. Full confidentiality and integrity loss of the ontology.\n\n1. Never honor test-principal headers on network-reachable deployments. Move the entire test-auth bypass out of `globalAuth`’s request path and behind an explicit, source-address-and-environment guard.\n2. Require BOTH `NODE_ENV` to be a non-production value **and** a distinct, rotation-capable shared secret (e.g. `TELLUS_TEST_HOOKS_SECRET`) that must accompany any test-auth assertion — never the flag alone.\n3. Add a source-address check (loopback only) mirroring `isLocalhost()` in `principal.ts` to both bypass branches in `globalAuth`; do not allow the header path to be more permissive than the code-repos fallback.\n4. Stop copying request-supplied roles verbatim; the principal builder should only accept a fixed allowlist of test users from `TEST_USER_SEEDS`, not arbitrary `userId`/role strings.\n5. Add a boot-time assertion that fails startup when `TELLUS_TEST_HOOKS=1` and the server is bound to a non-loopback interface, independent of `NODE_ENV`."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "9.8",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-489",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/489.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-248",
              "name": "CVE-2026-59892 in @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger 2.7.1 (unauthenticated DoS via malformed trace header)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59892 in @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger 2.7.1 (unauthenticated DoS via malformed trace header)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The transitive package **`@opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger@2.7.1`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-59892: `uber-trace-id` and `uberctx-*` HTTP header values are decoded with `decodeURIComponent()` without handling decode errors, so an **unauthenticated remote attacker** can send a malformed percent-encoded value that throws an uncaught `URIError` and terminates the Node.js process. This is a remotely triggerable DoS with no preconditions — the most directly attacker-relevant of the dependency findings. Fixed in `2.9.0`."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The transitive package **`@opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger@2.7.1`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-59892: `uber-trace-id` and `uberctx-*` HTTP header values are decoded with `decodeURIComponent()` without handling decode errors, so an **unauthenticated remote attacker** can send a malformed percent-encoded value that throws an uncaught `URIError` and terminates the Node.js process. This is a remotely triggerable DoS with no preconditions — the most directly attacker-relevant of the dependency findings. Fixed in `2.9.0`.\n\nAn unauthenticated remote client sends a malformed `uber-trace-id` / `uberctx-*` header; the propagator throws an uncaught `URIError` that terminates the Node.js process — a reliable remote DoS of the API server.\n\nResolve `@opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger@>=2.9.0` by bumping `@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node` / `@opentelemetry/sdk-node`, or `pnpm.overrides: { \"@opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger@<2.9.0\": \"^2.9.0\" }`. Regenerate lockfile, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`.",
                "markdown": "The transitive package **`@opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger@2.7.1`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-59892: `uber-trace-id` and `uberctx-*` HTTP header values are decoded with `decodeURIComponent()` without handling decode errors, so an **unauthenticated remote attacker** can send a malformed percent-encoded value that throws an uncaught `URIError` and terminates the Node.js process. This is a remotely triggerable DoS with no preconditions — the most directly attacker-relevant of the dependency findings. Fixed in `2.9.0`.\n\nAn unauthenticated remote client sends a malformed `uber-trace-id` / `uberctx-*` header; the propagator throws an uncaught `URIError` that terminates the Node.js process — a reliable remote DoS of the API server.\n\nResolve `@opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger@>=2.9.0` by bumping `@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node` / `@opentelemetry/sdk-node`, or `pnpm.overrides: { \"@opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger@<2.9.0\": \"^2.9.0\" }`. Regenerate lockfile, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-248",
                  "CVE-2026-59892",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/248.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54285",
              "name": "CVE-2026-54285 in @opentelemetry/core 2.7.x (DoS via oversized attributes)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-54285 in @opentelemetry/core 2.7.x (DoS via oversized attributes)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The transitive package **`@opentelemetry/core`** (two pinned copies: `2.7.0` and `2.7.1`, via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-54285: oversized span/log attributes cause a denial of service. Fixed in `2.8.0`."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The transitive package **`@opentelemetry/core`** (two pinned copies: `2.7.0` and `2.7.1`, via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-54285: oversized span/log attributes cause a denial of service. Fixed in `2.8.0`.\n\nOversized attributes cause low-severity DoS in the OpenTelemetry core used by the API's telemetry bootstrap.\n\nResolve `@opentelemetry/core@>=2.8.0` via `@opentelemetry/sdk-node` bump or `pnpm.overrides`; regenerate lockfile; verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`.",
                "markdown": "The transitive package **`@opentelemetry/core`** (two pinned copies: `2.7.0` and `2.7.1`, via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-54285: oversized span/log attributes cause a denial of service. Fixed in `2.8.0`.\n\nOversized attributes cause low-severity DoS in the OpenTelemetry core used by the API's telemetry bootstrap.\n\nResolve `@opentelemetry/core@>=2.8.0` via `@opentelemetry/sdk-node` bump or `pnpm.overrides`; regenerate lockfile; verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`."
              },
              "properties": {
