            {
              "id": "CWE-94",
              "name": "RCE: un-gated legacy ontology Function register+invoke escapes Node vm sandbox to host command execution",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RCE: un-gated legacy ontology Function register+invoke escapes Node vm sandbox to host command execution"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Any low-priv authenticated user (e.g. a **viewer**) can register an arbitrary TypeScript **Function** through the legacy ontology route and immediately invoke it, escaping the Node `vm` sandbox to execute arbitrary OS commands on the host as the API process user. The route carries **no** `authorizePublish()` gate, no transpile/import validation, and no audit — the publish-authorization boundary documented for the Functions executor is wired only to the canonical `/api/v1/functions/:rid/versions` and `/api/v1/code-repositories/:rid/tags` endpoints, not to this parallel legacy router."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Any low-priv authenticated user (e.g. a **viewer**) can register an arbitrary TypeScript **Function** through the legacy ontology route and immediately invoke it, escaping the Node `vm` sandbox to execute arbitrary OS commands on the host as the API process user. The route carries **no** `authorizePublish()` gate, no transpile/import validation, and no audit — the publish-authorization boundary documented for the Functions executor is wired only to the canonical `/api/v1/functions/:rid/versions` and `/api/v1/code-repositories/:rid/tags` endpoints, not to this parallel legacy router.\n\nA viewer-level principal achieves **remote code execution on the host running the API**: the PoC returned `uid=501(olivierhabimana) gid=20(staff)` and hostname `Olivier-HABIMANA.local` from `child_process.execSync` executed inside the \"sandboxed\" function, and `fs.writeFileSync` wrote/read a file on the host. The compromised process environment exposes database credentials — the sandbox read `PGPASSWORD` and `POSTGRES_URL` (plus `PGUSER`/`PGDATABASE`/`PGHOST`) — enabling full compromise of the ontology database and lateral movement. Any tenant user with valid credentials can take over the API host identity.\n\n1. Immediately gate the legacy route: require `authorizePublish()` (the same gate used by `/api/v1/functions/:repositoryRid/versions`) plus ontology-ownership/superadmin checks on `POST /`, `POST /:apiName/versions`, and `POST /:apiName/invoke` — or decommission the legacy router entirely now that the canonical Functions registry exists.\n2. Never execute untrusted source in-process: remove the in-process `runSandboxed` path for user-supplied code and route all invocation through the worker-pool executor (`src/services/functionWorkerPool.ts`) so user code runs outside the API event loop with an env whitelist.\n3. Add a defense-in-depth escape guard: reject/route-around sources reachable to the host `Function` constructor (e.g. freeze/neuter `constructor` chains on the sandbox global, or run under a real isolate such as `isolated-vm`/Firecracker), and validate imports/AST at publish time.\n4. Add a CI assertion that no code-registration or code-invocation route exists without publish authorization + audit.",
                "markdown": "Any low-priv authenticated user (e.g. a **viewer**) can register an arbitrary TypeScript **Function** through the legacy ontology route and immediately invoke it, escaping the Node `vm` sandbox to execute arbitrary OS commands on the host as the API process user. The route carries **no** `authorizePublish()` gate, no transpile/import validation, and no audit — the publish-authorization boundary documented for the Functions executor is wired only to the canonical `/api/v1/functions/:rid/versions` and `/api/v1/code-repositories/:rid/tags` endpoints, not to this parallel legacy router.\n\nA viewer-level principal achieves **remote code execution on the host running the API**: the PoC returned `uid=501(olivierhabimana) gid=20(staff)` and hostname `Olivier-HABIMANA.local` from `child_process.execSync` executed inside the \"sandboxed\" function, and `fs.writeFileSync` wrote/read a file on the host. The compromised process environment exposes database credentials — the sandbox read `PGPASSWORD` and `POSTGRES_URL` (plus `PGUSER`/`PGDATABASE`/`PGHOST`) — enabling full compromise of the ontology database and lateral movement. Any tenant user with valid credentials can take over the API host identity.\n\n1. Immediately gate the legacy route: require `authorizePublish()` (the same gate used by `/api/v1/functions/:repositoryRid/versions`) plus ontology-ownership/superadmin checks on `POST /`, `POST /:apiName/versions`, and `POST /:apiName/invoke` — or decommission the legacy router entirely now that the canonical Functions registry exists.\n2. Never execute untrusted source in-process: remove the in-process `runSandboxed` path for user-supplied code and route all invocation through the worker-pool executor (`src/services/functionWorkerPool.ts`) so user code runs outside the API event loop with an env whitelist.\n3. Add a defense-in-depth escape guard: reject/route-around sources reachable to the host `Function` constructor (e.g. freeze/neuter `constructor` chains on the sandbox global, or run under a real isolate such as `isolated-vm`/Firecracker), and validate imports/AST at publish time.\n4. Add a CI assertion that no code-registration or code-invocation route exists without publish authorization + audit."
              },
