      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-918",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-69192 in ip-address 10.1.0 (SSRF via inconsistent IPv4 parsing)\n\nThe transitive package **`ip-address@10.1.0`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-69192: `Address4` decodes IPv4 octets with a leading zero as **decimal**, whereas the WHATWG URL host parser, `inet_aton`, and `getaddrinfo` decode them as **octal**. The library and the network stack disagree about which host a string names, enabling SSRF and trust-boundary bypass when `ip-address` is used to validate destination hosts. Fixed in `10.3.1`. Published 2026-08-03; references include the upstream fix commit `beaugunderson/ip-address@56368cb` and Red Hat CVE advisory."
          },
