              "target": "/workspace/tellus",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-69192",
              "cwe": "CWE-918",
              "impact": "An attacker who can influence any host/IP validation performed through this chain can craft an address (e.g. `012.0.0.1`, `0x0a.1`) that the library validates as a benign/internal host while the actual DNS/connect layer resolves it to an arbitrary target, bypassing SSRF host allow/deny checks. Scope is Changed because the parsing confusion crosses a security authority boundary between validation and resolution.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** `ip-address` ≤ 10.1.0 treats an IPv4 octet written with a leading zero (e.g. `012`) as base-10. The WHATWG host parser, libc `inet_aton`, and `getaddrinfo` treat it as octal.  `new Address4('012.0.0.1')` therefore returns a different address than the one the network stack will actually connect to. Any validation/allowlist built on `ip-address` can be bypassed by an attacker-controlled host string.\n\n**Dependency chain observed in `pnpm-lock.yaml` (trivy `--list-all-pkgs` graph):**\n```\n@kubernetes/client-node@1.4.0(encoding@0.1.13)\n  > socks-proxy-agent@8.0.5\n    > socks@2.8.7\n      > ip-address@10.1.0\n```\nApplication code reaches `@kubernetes/client-node` via dynamic `import()` (lazy load) in `src/services/pipelines/udfRunner.ts:56` and `src/services/orchestration/runners/k8s-runtime.ts:61`, so the chain is loaded at runtime in k8s-enabled deployments.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nTarget=pnpm-lock.yaml  Type=pnpm  Class=lang-pkgs\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-69192  PkgName=ip-address  InstalledVersion=10.1.0  FixedVersion=10.3.1  Severity=HIGH\nCVSS redhat:8.6 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N)  CWE-20 / CWE-918\nPrimaryURL=https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-69192\n```\n\nThe direct dependency it rolls up to is `@kubernetes/client-node@1.4.0` (confirmed in `package.json`).",
              "remediation_steps": "The fix version `ip-address@10.3.1` is a *minor* bump within the range that `socks@2.8.7` declares (`^10.0.0`), so re-resolving the lockfile will pick it up automatically. Options:\n1. Bump the **direct** dependency in `package.json`: raise `@kubernetes/client-node` to a version whose closure pins `ip-address@>=10.3.1` (≥ 1.4.x patch that vendors the fix), then `pnpm install`.\n2. Add a pnpm override to force the transitive resolution, then commit the updated `pnpm-lock.yaml`:\n   `pnpm.overrides: { \"ip-address@<10.3.1\": \"^10.3.1\" }` in `package.json`.\n3. Re-run `pnpm install` and confirm with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml` that `ip-address` resolves to `>=10.3.1`.\nDo not edit `pnpm-lock.yaml` by hand; use `pnpm.overrides` so the lockfile stays reproducible.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "ip-address",
                "installed_version": "10.1.0",
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "pnpm-lock.yaml",
                "fixed_version": "10.3.1",
                "introduced_by": "@kubernetes/client-node@1.4.0",
                "dependency_path": "@kubernetes/client-node@1.4.0 > socks-proxy-agent@8.0.5 > socks@2.8.7 > ip-address@10.1.0",
                "reachability": "imported",
                "reachability_evidence": "Direct import search for `ip-address` returned no matches in `src/` or `scripts/` (`rg -n \"require\\(['\\\"]ip-address|from ['\\\"]ip-address\"` across `--type ts`). The package is only reached transitively through `@kubernetes/client-node` (confirmed dynamic `await import(\"@kubernetes/client-node\")` in src/services/pipelines/udfRunner.ts:56 and src/services/orchestration/runners/k8s-runtime.ts:61). The affected-symbol check (Address4 / Address6 signature use inside the k8s client-chain) was not performed."
              }
            }
          }
