              "cve": "CVE-2026-41907",
              "cwe": "CWE-787",
              "impact": "If `uuid.v5` (or v3/v6) is ever invoked with a caller-controlled output buffer and offset, the caller can coerce a write outside the intended buffer range, corrupting adjacent Node.js process memory. This is a memory-corruption primitive with integrity impact; the current application code paths do not pass the optional buf/offset arguments, so exploitation would require a future change or a dependency-chain caller.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** `uuid` prior to the fix does not bounds-check the optional `(buf, offset)` out-params on `v3`/`v5`/`v6`. Passing a `buf` that is too small or an `offset` larger than the buffer silently writes out of range.\n\n**Application usage:** `uuid@^13.0.0` is a direct dependency in `package.json`. Import scan found:\n- `src/config/foundryMulter.ts:4` — `v4` (not affected)\n- `src/middleware/correlationId.ts:2` — `v4` (not affected)\n- `src/services/branchContext.ts:22,44` — `v5` (**affected API**, but called as `uuidv5(name, DNS_NS)` with no `buf`/`offset`)\n- `src/services/quiver/rids.ts:11` — `v7` (not affected)\n\nThe vulnerable `v5` symbol is used, so per the evidence ladder this is `vulnerable_symbol_used`, but the specific OOB-write invocation pattern is not present in existing code.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nTarget=pnpm-lock.yaml  Type=pnpm  Class=lang-pkgs\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-41907  PkgName=uuid  InstalledVersion=13.0.0  FixedVersion=11.1.1, 12.0.1, 13.0.1  Severity=MEDIUM\nCVSS ghsa:7.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N)  CWE-787 / CWE-823\n```\n\n`uuid` is a direct dependency, so no `introduced_by` chain applies.",
              "remediation_steps": "Bump the direct dependency: raise `\"uuid\"` in `package.json` from `^13.0.0` to `^13.0.1` (or `^14.0.0`), run `pnpm install`, and verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml` that the resolved version is `>=13.0.1`. Because `^13.0.0` already permits `13.0.1`, a plain `pnpm update uuid` may pick the fix without editing `package.json`; committing the regenerated lockfile is sufficient. No code changes are required.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "uuid",
                "installed_version": "13.0.0",
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "pnpm-lock.yaml",
                "fixed_version": "13.0.1",
                "reachability": "vulnerable_symbol_used",
                "reachability_evidence": "The affected symbol `uuid.v5` IS imported and used by application code: `src/services/branchContext.ts:22` (`import { v5 as uuidv5 } from \"uuid\"`) and called at `src/services/branchContext.ts:44` as `uuidv5(`${ontologyId}:main`, DNS_NS)`. However, the vulnerable code path requires the optional `buf`/`offset` arguments; the current call sites pass only `(name, namespace)` with no caller-provided buffer, so the OOB-write primitive is not exercised by existing code. Direct `uuid` imports confirmed at src/config/foundryMulter.ts:4, src/middleware/correlationId.ts:2 (both `v4`, unaffected), src/services/quiver/rids.ts:11 (`v7`, unaffected)."
