        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-436",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-13676 in fast-uri 3.1.2 via ajv (URL security-policy bypass via Unicode hostname canonicalization)\n\nThe transitive package **`fast-uri@3.1.2`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `ajv`) is affected by CVE-2026-13676: `fast-uri` versions 2.3.1 through 3.1.2 and 4.0.0 fail to canonicalize Unicode (IDN) hostnames for HTTP-family URLs — the IDN conversion path calls a helper that does not exist on the global `URL` constructor — so `normalize()` / `equal()` return values that differ from a WHATWG-compatible URL parser. Applications using `fast-uri` (directly or via `ajv`'s URI format validation) to enforce hostname policy can be bypassed. Fixed in `3.1.3` / `4.0.1` / `2.4.2`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
