          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-16221 in fast-uri 3.1.2 via ajv (URL security-policy bypass — backslash not treated as authority delimiter)\n\nThe transitive package **`fast-uri@3.1.2`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `ajv`) is affected by CVE-2026-16221: versions 2.3.1 through 4.1.0 do not treat a literal backslash (U+005C) as an authority delimiter, whereas Node's native WHATWG URL parser (used by `fetch`, `undici`, `http`) normalizes `\\` to `/` for special schemes. A URL that ajv/fast-uri validates as one origin can resolve to a different host at fetch time, bypassing URI-format/security policy. Fixed in `3.1.4` / `4.1.1` / `2.4.3`."
          },
          "locations": [
