          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-18446 in fast-uri 3.1.2 via ajv (host confusion — backslash collapses authority into path)\n\nThe transitive package **`fast-uri@3.1.2`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `ajv`) is affected by CVE-2026-18446: fast-uri requires a literal `//` to recognize a URI authority, so a reference that uses a backslash-based introducer (`\\\\`, `\\/`, `/\\`) is parsed with **no authority and folds into the path**, whereas Node's WHATWG parser treats `\\` as interchangeable with `/` and still extracts the authority caller-provided data. Validated origin and fetched origin diverge. Fixed in `3.1.5` / `4.1.2` / `2.4.4`. References include upstream fix commit `fastify/fast-uri@f3c6c90`."
          },
