              "cve": "CVE-2026-18446",
              "cwe": "CWE-436",
              "impact": "Host-confusion: an attacker URL that fast-uri validates against one origin (or as relative) is fetched by Node's network stack as belonging to a different, attacker-chosen host. This can defeat SSRF/origin host allowlists enforced through any ajv/fast-uri-based validation, with Integrity impact.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** fast-uri < 3.1.5 / 4.1.2 / 2.4.4 requires literal `//` for an authority; a `\\`-introduced authority is folded into the path, but the WHATWG parser keeps the authority. Validation and resolution disagree on the effective host.\n\n**Dependency chain (`pnpm-lock.yaml`):** `ajv@8.18.0 > fast-uri@3.1.2`. `ajv@8.18.0` direct in `package.json`; used at `src/services/workshop/validator.ts:48`.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-18446  PkgName=fast-uri  InstalledVersion=3.1.2  FixedVersion=2.4.4, 3.1.5, 4.1.2  Severity=HIGH\nCVSS ghsa:7.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N)  CWE-436\nPrimaryURL=https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-18446\n```\nThird distinct fast-uri mechanism filed for this manifest (see also vuln-0004 CVE-2026-13676 IDN, vuln-0005 CVE-2026-16221 authority delimiter).",
              "remediation_steps": "Same single fix covers all three fast-uri CVEs: resolve `fast-uri >= 3.1.5`.\n1. Bump the direct `ajv` dependency to a version whose closure pulls `fast-uri@>=3.1.5`, then `pnpm install`; or\n2. `pnpm.overrides: { \"fast-uri@<3.1.5\": \"^3.1.5\" }` in `package.json`.\n3. Commit the lockfile and confirm with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`.",
