              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** js-yaml ≤ 4.2.0 (4.x) / 3.x merge-key resolution has an algorithmic-complexity flaw producing O(n²) CPU on adversarial documents.\n\n**Dependency chain (`pnpm-lock.yaml`):**\n```\n@kubernetes/client-node@1.4.0(encoding@0.1.13) > js-yaml@4.2.0\n```\nThe direct dep `@kubernetes/client-node` is confirmed in `package.json` and lazy-loaded in the k8s runtime paths.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-59869  PkgName=js-yaml  InstalledVersion=4.2.0  FixedVersion=3.15.0, 4.3.0  Severity=HIGH\nCVSS ghsa:7.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H)  CWE-407\n```\nA sibling GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj (the `!!omap` O(n²) issue) is also present on the same package but has **no mapped CVE id** and per scan policy is not reported via create_dependency_report.",
