            "text": "CVE-2026-39244 in adm-zip 0.5.16 (DoS via crafted ZIP — unbounded memory from spoofed size header)\n\nThe direct dependency **`adm-zip@0.5.16`** (declared in `package.json` and pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml`) is affected by CVE-2026-39244: `zipEntry.js` line 103 allocates `Buffer.alloc(_centralHeader.size)` from the ZIP central-directory declared uncompressed size **without validating it against the actual compressed data or imposing an upper bound**, so a crafted ZIP with a manipulated size header causes excessive memory allocation and denial of service. Fixed in `0.6.0`. References: upstream commit `cthackers/adm-zip@2450dcf`, issue #568, Red Hat CVE advisory."
