          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "5743181493c9bf9c378a767eb9c2bee8704221d39e630e3b082619f0a6440f02",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0009",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 6.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-18 06:37:49 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:3000",
              "endpoint": "/api/v1/audit/log",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-862",
              "impact": "Any authenticated principal, including an account with no assigned business roles (`realm_access.roles = ['offline_access','marking:PUBLIC','default-roles-tellus']`), can read the complete cross-user audit trail. The PoC returned **21,252 audit entries** containing other users' internal user UUIDs (`executedBy`), client IPs (`sourceIp`), and full business parameters of their actions (loan application primary keys such as `QA-RW-BK-L-0000048`, credit-decision `rationale` and `approvedLimit` values, results, and error messages). The file header for this route states the audit log is \"legally mandatory — every data modification must be traceable\", i.e. it is compliance/security data intended for administrators and auditors only. This is a privacy and regulatory exposure (mass disclosure of who did what, when, from where, across the whole system), and it also aids further attacks by revealing valid object primary keys, user IDs, and internal error details.",
              "technical_analysis": "The three global audit handlers invoke the audit query path directly, with no authorization middleware between the router and the handler. `globalAuditRouter.get` is called with only a path and the async handler:\n\n```typescript title=src/routes/auditLog.ts startLineNumber=280 endLineNumber=282\nglobalAuditRouter.get(\n  \"/log\",\n  async (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n```\n\nThe router is mounted in `src/server.ts` with no guard either: `app.use(\"/api/v1/audit\", globalAuditRouter);`. The `globalAuth` middleware applied earlier in the stack only verifies that a valid JWT is present (authentication); it performs no role/permission evaluation. Per the project's own route-map analysis, \"Routes with NO route-level authz beyond globalAuth: POST /api/v1/sql, /api/v1/audit.\" The SQL built by `queryAuditLog()` is parameterized (no SQL injection), so the issue is purely the missing function-level authorization. The same codebase already demonstrates the correct pattern: `POST /api/v1/sql/invalidate` in `src/routes/sql.ts` is wrapped with `authorize('ontology-admin')` imported from `src/middleware/auth.ts`.",
              "remediation_steps": "Wrap every global audit handler in the existing `authorize` middleware from `src/middleware/auth`, restricted to `ontology-admin` (or a dedicated `auditor` role), mirroring the pattern already used for `POST /api/v1/sql/invalidate` in `src/routes/sql.ts`. Concretely, import `authorize` and add it as the second argument to each of the three `globalAuditRouter.get(...)` registrations (`/log`, `/log/:executionId`, `/stats`). Additionally, scope `executedBy` to the caller for non-admin users if per-user self-audit visibility is ever desired, and keep the action-scoped `actionAuditRouter` consistent with the same authorization decision. Add regression tests asserting a JWT with no business role receives HTTP 403 on all three endpoints, and that an `ontology-admin` JWT receives HTTP 200.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Mint a JWT for the zero-role seeded user `cypress-nogroups@tellus.local` via the Keycloak token endpoint (realm `tellus`, public client `tellus-frontend`, forcing `Host: localhost:8086` so the `iss` claim matches the API allowlist).\n2. Decode the JWT and confirm `realm_access.roles` contains no business role (`['offline_access','marking:PUBLIC','default-roles-tellus']`).\n3. Send `GET /api/v1/audit/log?pageSize=1` with the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.\n4. Observe HTTP 200 with `totalCount: 21252` and a row exposing another user's `executedBy` UUID, `sourceIp`, and action `parameters`.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-776",
