            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0010",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-18 06:38:28 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/tellus",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-33036",
              "cwe": "CWE-776",
              "impact": "A crafted XML document (entity expansion) parsed through the AWS SDK's XML builder can cause unbounded memory/CPU consumption despite the supposed expansion limits, hanging the event loop. Availability impact only; reachable when the S3 client parses XML responses.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** fast-xml-parser 4.0.0-beta.3 through 5.5.5 — the expansion-limit guards added for CVE-2026-26278 are bypassed by numeric character references and standard entities, restoring entity-expansion DoS.\n\n**Dependency chain (`pnpm-lock.yaml`):**\n```\n@aws-sdk/client-s3@3.1010.0\n  > @aws-sdk/core@3.973.20\n    > @aws-sdk/xml-builder@3.972.11\n      > fast-xml-parser@5.4.1\n```\n`@aws-sdk/client-s3@3.1010.0` is a direct dependency used by the app's S3/MinIO storage layer.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-33036  PkgName=fast-xml-parser  InstalledVersion=5.4.1  FixedVersion=5.5.6, 4.5.5  Severity=HIGH\nCVSS ghsa:7.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H)  CWE-776\n```\nTwo further fast-xml-parser CVEs (CVE-2026-33349 unbounded entity expansion, CVE-2026-41650 XML-injection) affect the same pinned copy; this report covers CVE-2026-33036 specifically.",
              "remediation_steps": "The package is transitive AND already behind a `pnpm.overrides` pin, so update the override ceiling:\n1. Edit `package.json` `pnpm.overrides` to raise the floor/ceiling: `\"fast-xml-parser@<5.5.6\": \"5.5.6\"` (or widen to also bump 4.x: `\"fast-xml-parser@>=4.0.0 <5.5.6\": \"5.5.6\"` and keep a `4.5.5` pin if any consumer is locked to 4.x).\n2. `pnpm install` to regenerate `pnpm-lock.yaml`.\n3. Confirm with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml` that all `fast-xml-parser` copies are at fixed versions (≥5.5.6 / ≥4.5.5). Alternatively bump `@aws-sdk/client-s3` to a release whose closure resolves a fixed fast-xml-parser.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "fast-xml-parser",
                "installed_version": "5.4.1",
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "pnpm-lock.yaml",
                "fixed_version": "5.5.6",
                "introduced_by": "@aws-sdk/client-s3@3.1010.0",
                "dependency_path": "@aws-sdk/client-s3@3.1010.0 > @aws-sdk/core@3.973.20 > @aws-sdk/xml-builder@3.972.11 > fast-xml-parser@5.4.1",
                "reachability": "imported",
                "reachability_evidence": "No application code imports `fast-xml-parser` directly (`rg -n \"require\\(['\\\"]fast-xml-parser|from ['\\\"]fast-xml-parser\"` over `--type ts` on src/ returned no hits). Reached via `@aws-sdk/client-s3` (direct dep, used by S3 storage code throughout `src/services`). The app's `package.json` already has `pnpm.overrides` forcing `fast-xml-parser@<5.4.1 → 5.4.1`, confirming the team actively pins this package. Affected-symbol (parser entity-handling) check inside the AWS SDK chain was not performed."
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 8,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "IDOR: authenticated users read arbitrary projects and dataset file contents (dataset RBAC disabled by default + default-org auto-enroll voids project read isolation)\n\nThe Ontology Engine's dataset read endpoints (`GET /api/v1/datasets/:datasetId`, `/preview`, `/download`, `/status`, `/summary`) and project read endpoints (`GET /api/v1/projects/:id`, `/:id/stats`, `/:id/folders`, `/:id/datasets/all`, `/:id/members`) enforce no object-level authorization. Any authenticated user — even one with zero roles and no project membership — can read arbitrary projects and exfiltrate the full contents of any uploaded dataset file by direct object ID (IDOR / Broken Object-Level Authorization). Only write operations are correctly gated."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/services/datasetAcl.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 208,
                  "endLine": 209
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Fail-closed per-dataset RBAC (secure-by-default)"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/routes/foundryDatasets.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 31,
                  "endLine": 36,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export const datasetRouter = Router();\n// Function-level authorization on the by-id dataset surface (the IDOR\n// vector): update (PUT) requires ontology-editor, delete requires\n// ontology-admin, and write-POSTs (duplicate/reparse) require editor. Reads\n// (get/preview/download/status/summary) stay open. PATs are scope-gated\n// upstream (datasets:* scopes); superadmin passes.\ndatasetRouter.use(dataPlaneGuard({ post: 'write' }));"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Guarded dataset read surface (dataPlaneGuard GET passthrough context)"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/services/projectService.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 127,
                  "endLine": 134
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Require project membership for listProjects instead of org overlap"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/v1/datasets/:datasetId/download",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/services/datasetAcl.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 208,
                        "endLine": 209
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "// callers. Disable explicitly with DATASET_RBAC_ENABLED=false (NOT recommended).\n  return (process.env.DATASET_RBAC_ENABLED ?? \"true\").toLowerCase() === \"true\";"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/services/projectService.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 127,
                        "endLine": 134
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "async listProjects(ownerId: string, fields?: string[]) {\n    const query = this.knex('projects').where((qb) => {\n      qb.where({ owner_id: ownerId }).orWhereExists(this.projectMembership(ownerId));\n    });\n    if (fields && fields.length > 0) {\n      query.select(fields.map(f => `projects.${f}`));\n    }\n    return query.orderBy('updated_at', 'desc');\n  }\n\n  // Projects the user is an explicit member of (project_members), not merely\n  // org-overlapping. Org overlap alone is NOT sufficient for read access.\n  private projectMembership(userId: string) {\n    return this.knex('project_members')\n      .select(this.knex.raw('1'))\n      .whereRaw('project_members.project_id = projects.id')\n      .where('project_members.user_id', userId);\n  }"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "1. Gate ALL dataset read routes on object-level authorization by making per-dataset RBAC fail-closed: default `DATASET_RBAC_ENABLED` to true (or remove the opt-in entirely) so `effectiveRole()` is always enforced and a null role returns 403.\n2. Stop auto-enrolling every user and every project into a single shared default org; only enroll entities into real orgs they actually belong to.\n3. Change `ProjectService.listProjects` / `getProjectById` (and the folder/dataset/members/stats reads that inherit them) to require `project_members` membership or an explicit share grant rather than org overlap; treat org overlap as additive to membership, never a replacement for it.\n4. Add integration tests asserting that a non-member / zero-role user receives 403/404 on project and dataset reads, so the boundary cannot silently regress to fail-open.",
                "markdown": "1. Gate ALL dataset read routes on object-level authorization by making per-dataset RBAC fail-closed: default `DATASET_RBAC_ENABLED` to true (or remove the opt-in entirely) so `effectiveRole()` is always enforced and a null role returns 403.\n2. Stop auto-enrolling every user and every project into a single shared default org; only enroll entities into real orgs they actually belong to.\n3. Change `ProjectService.listProjects` / `getProjectById` (and the folder/dataset/members/stats reads that inherit them) to require `project_members` membership or an explicit share grant rather than org overlap; treat org overlap as additive to membership, never a replacement for it.\n4. Add integration tests asserting that a non-member / zero-role user receives 403/404 on project and dataset reads, so the boundary cannot silently regress to fail-open."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "d93faf4cec34f8ea4a06f05f7624c67b3053631df746974de2b6c492ad35fbcd"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "ebf1ba63c404f36a89caddaa6fe5f69242fcb30f0ba18d9b0a595b1226f560fa",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0011",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 6.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-18 06:39:32 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:3000",
              "endpoint": "/api/v1/datasets/:datasetId/download",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-639",
              "impact": "Full contents of any uploaded dataset file are readable cross-user by any holder of a valid bearer token. Project metadata (owner, members' emails/roles), folder trees, datasets lists, stats, and summaries for arbitrary projects are likewise exposed. Confidentiality of all stored file data is broken; only integrity is preserved because write paths (PUT/DELETE project, POST folder/members, upload) correctly return 403/404 for the same actor. No special role, project membership, or org sharing is required beyond authentication.",
              "technical_analysis": "Root cause is two-part.\n\n**Part A — dataset by-id reads have no object-level authorization by default.**\n`src/routes/foundryDatasets.ts:36` mounts `datasetRouter.use(dataPlaneGuard({ post: 'write' }))`. In `src/middleware/requireRole.ts:150-160`, `dataPlaneGuard` short-circuits ALL GET/HEAD/OPTIONS with an immediate `next()` — it only gates DELETE (ontology-admin) and POST/PUT/PATCH (ontology-write). Reads therefore pass with no principal/object binding. The only object-level guard is `requireDatasetRole('viewer')` on routes lines 43-50, but it is OPT-IN: `src/services/datasetAcl.ts:208-209` `isDatasetRbacEnabled()` returns true only when `process.env.DATASET_RBAC_ENABLED === 'true'`; it defaults to `\"false\"` and is not set in `.env` or any docker-compose file. When disabled the middleware no-ops (`if (!isDatasetRbacEnabled()) return next();`). Net effect: dataset reads are authenticated-but-unauthorized → IDOR.\n\n**Part B — the project/folder membership read-boundary is a no-op.**\n`src/services/projectService.ts:127-129` `listProjects` and `:146-160` `getProjectById` use `orgSharedProjects()` / an EXISTS subquery joining `project_organizations`↔`user_organizations`. But `src/foundryMigrate.ts` (B4 Step 19 backfill ~1264-1271 and Step 19b auto-enroll triggers ~1289-1315) seeds ONE shared org `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001` (\"default\") and auto-enrolls EVERY user and EVERY project into it via `enroll_user_default_org()` and `enroll_project_default_org()` AFTER INSERT triggers. The org-membership EXISTS predicate is therefore trivially true for every (user, project) pair — \"org-shared read\" is effectively global read, and project-based reads (`/folders`, `/datasets/all`, `/members`, `/stats`) inherit it.\n\nWrites remain correctly gated by `authorizeRoles('owner'/'editor')` and `owner_id` checks in ProjectService/FolderService, confirming the read-side org shortcut was never meant to be the enforcement point.\n\nBoth a zero-role user (`cypress-nogroups@tellus.local`, realm_access.roles = only `offline_access` + `default-roles-tellus`, not in `project_members`, in no legitimate shared org) and a `marking:PUBLIC`-viewer context were validated; the IDOR reproduces for both against the admin's private project `f33e3cec-2676-416f-a095-04e3de11f2ed`.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Gate ALL dataset read routes on object-level authorization by making per-dataset RBAC fail-closed: default `DATASET_RBAC_ENABLED` to true (or remove the opt-in entirely) so `effectiveRole()` is always enforced and a null role returns 403.\n2. Stop auto-enrolling every user and every project into a single shared default org; only enroll entities into real orgs they actually belong to.\n3. Change `ProjectService.listProjects` / `getProjectById` (and the folder/dataset/members/stats reads that inherit them) to require `project_members` membership or an explicit share grant rather than org overlap; treat org overlap as additive to membership, never a replacement for it.\n4. Add integration tests asserting that a non-member / zero-role user receives 403/404 on project and dataset reads, so the boundary cannot silently regress to fail-open.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. As admin, create a private project and note its project id (victim: `f33e3cec-2676-416f-a095-04e3de11f2ed`).\n2. As admin, upload a CSV (e.g. `admin-secret.csv`) so it becomes a dataset (id `5f8376fa-ae7a-4a2e-95c6-d71da62ba247`).\n3. Mint a bearer token for a non-member, zero-role user (`cypress-nogroups@tellus.local`) from Keycloak (realm `tellus`, client `tellus-frontend`).\n4. As that user, `GET /api/v1/projects/{projectId}` → HTTP 200 with full project JSON including `owner_id`.\n5. `GET /api/v1/projects/{projectId}/datasets/all` → HTTP 200 listing the admin's dataset.\n6. `GET /api/v1/datasets/{datasetId}/preview` → HTTP 200 returning row data containing `SECRET` / `TOP` / `ADMIN_DATA`.\n7. `GET /api/v1/datasets/{datasetId}/download` → HTTP 200 returning the raw file body verbatim.\n8. `GET /api/v1/projects/{projectId}/members` → HTTP 200 revealing the admin's email and owner role.\n9. Contrast: attempt `PUT /api/v1/projects/{projectId}` as the same user → HTTP 403 FORBIDDEN, proving writes are gated and the flaw is read-only.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 9,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated system-status endpoints leak infrastructure and business-schema inventory\n\nThe endpoints `GET /api/v1/system/health` and `GET /health/detailed` respond with no authentication and disclose a full infrastructure and business-schema inventory: the PostgreSQL server version, per-table row counts, the live OpenSearch cluster name and node count, all 80 index names with per-index document counts and sizes, a 121-entry object-type inventory (apiName, propertyCount, objectCount, lastIndexed, indexStatus) that exposes client business domains, host memory footprint, database reachability, and uptime."
