              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "1. Split the health surface into two routers: a minimal liveness/readiness router returning only `{status, timestamp}` (kept unauthenticated for Kubernetes probes) and a detailed/system router for diagnostics.\n2. Gate the detailed/system endpoints behind authentication: remove `/api/v1/system/health` from the globalAuth allowlist (keep only `/liveness` and `/readiness`) and add an authentication middleware to the system-health and health-detailed handlers, or mount those routers after `globalAuth` runs.\n3. Reduce the payload of the system-health response: return aggregate counts only, and drop the object-type `apiName` and index `name` strings (per-type/per-index names must never appear in an unauthenticated response) or require an authorized viewer/operator role for the detailed breakdown.\n4. Remove process memory figures from any unauthenticated response.",
                "markdown": "1. Split the health surface into two routers: a minimal liveness/readiness router returning only `{status, timestamp}` (kept unauthenticated for Kubernetes probes) and a detailed/system router for diagnostics.\n2. Gate the detailed/system endpoints behind authentication: remove `/api/v1/system/health` from the globalAuth allowlist (keep only `/liveness` and `/readiness`) and add an authentication middleware to the system-health and health-detailed handlers, or mount those routers after `globalAuth` runs.\n3. Reduce the payload of the system-health response: return aggregate counts only, and drop the object-type `apiName` and index `name` strings (per-type/per-index names must never appear in an unauthenticated response) or require an authorized viewer/operator role for the detailed breakdown.\n4. Remove process memory figures from any unauthenticated response."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "b9f93997ed886978ce8f86cdbf6246c3f39b86cd8f9050642c97eab8dd42bd36"
