              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** unbounded entity expansion in fast-xml-parser ≤ 5.5.6 (this CVE) — a separate flaw from the numeric-character-reference limit bypass of CVE-2026-33036.\n\n**Dependency chain (`pnpm-lock.yaml`):** `@aws-sdk/client-s3@3.1010.0 > @aws-sdk/core@3.973.20 > @aws-sdk/xml-builder@3.972.11 > fast-xml-parser@5.4.1`.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-33349  PkgName=fast-xml-parser  InstalledVersion=5.4.1  FixedVersion=5.5.7, 4.5.5  Severity=MEDIUM\nCVSS:5.9 (AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H)\n```",
              "remediation_steps": "Resolve `fast-xml-parser` to `>=5.5.7` (also fixes CVE-2026-33036). Update `package.json` `pnpm.overrides` to `\"fast-xml-parser@<5.5.7\": \"5.5.7\"`, `pnpm install`, commit lockfile, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
