              "impact": "XML injection: an attacker-controlled string serialized through the XML builder (e.g. an S3 object metadata value) can inject additional XML elements/structure into the produced document, producing a low-integrity impact on the serialized output. No direct confidentiality/availability effect.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** fast-xml-parser ≤ 5.6.x does not correctly escape XML comments and CDATA when serializing, allowing XML injection. Distinct mechanism from the two entity-expansion DoS CVEs on the same package.\n\n**Dependency chain (`pnpm-lock.yaml`):** `@aws-sdk/client-s3@3.1010.0 > @aws-sdk/core@3.973.20 > @aws-sdk/xml-builder@3.972.11 > fast-xml-parser@5.4.1`.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-41650  PkgName=fast-xml-parser  InstalledVersion=5.4.1  FixedVersion=5.7.0  Severity=MEDIUM\nCVSS:6.1  CWE-91 (implied by XML injection class)\n```",
              "remediation_steps": "Resolve `fast-xml-parser` to `**6.1**` is the CVE published score but the fix line that also clears the other two fast-xml-parser CVEs is `>=5.7.0`: update `package.json` `pnpm.overrides` to `\"fast-xml-parser@<5.7.0\": \"5.7.0\"`, `pnpm install`, commit lockfile, and verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`. Note `5.7.0 >= 5.5.7`, so this single bump also clears CVE-2026-33036 and CVE-2026-33349.",
