          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-59873 in tar 7.5.13 via duckdb (DoS via crafted gzip bomb — no decompressed-size cap)\n\nThe transitive package **`tar@7.5.13`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `duckdb`'s `@mapbox/node-pre-gyp`) is affected by CVE-2026-59873: node-tar does not enforce hard upper bounds on total decompressed data, entry counts, or decompression ratio in extraction/parsing paths (`src/extract.ts`), so a small crafted gzip bomb can exhaust disk space and CPU. Fixed in `7.5.19`. This is the highest-severity of the tar CVEs on this pinned copy (severity CRITICAL per trivy, advisory vector 7.5 A:H). References: Red Hat errata RHSA-2026:47058/:47060."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
