          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "3e9ce99b92535bf5f9bb10a2cf984351d6ccb6b9b42a23efda045e312eab4a54"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "610fead7733f7b02680fb0c337937706c7ccecfd6571ae588089f98dafb64303",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0015",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-18 06:40:41 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/tellus",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-59873",
              "cwe": "CWE-770",
              "impact": "A crafted tar/gzip archive without decompressed-size limits can consume unbounded disk and CPU. In this project the `tar` code sits behind `duckdb`'s binary-delivery (`@mapbox/node-pre-gyp` downloads a prebuilt duckdb native binary as a tarball at package install/rebuild), so the realistic trigger is a compromised or hostile binary-distribution channel rather than direct end-user input — an availability-destructive primitive in the build/runtime bootstrap path.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** node-tar < 7.5.19 places no hard caps on decompressed total size, entry count, or expansion ratio in `extract`/parse paths, enabling gzip-bomb exhaustion.\n\n**Dependency chain (`pnpm-lock.yaml`):**\n```\nduckdb@1.4.4(encoding@0.1.13) > @mapbox/node-pre-gyp@2.0.3 > tar@7.5.13\n```\n`duckdb@1.4.4` is a direct dependency in `package.json` and is `require`d in `src/services/furnaceSqlService.ts:55` and `src/services/duckdb/pool.ts:49`. `@mapbox/node-pre-gyp` is the binary-fetch layer that uses `tar` to unpack the prebuilt duckdb native binding.\n\n**Trivy excerpt:**\n```\nVulnerabilityID=CVE-2026-59873  PkgName=tar  InstalledVersion=7.5.13  FixedVersion=7.5.19  Severity=CRITICAL\nCVSS ghsa:7.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H)  CWE-770\n```\nOther tar CVEs on the same pinned copy (CVE-2026-59874, CVE-2026-59871, CVE-2026-59875, CVE-2026-53655) are filed separately.",
              "remediation_steps": "`tar` is transitive (under `duckdb`), so fix at the direct level or via override:\n1. Bump the direct `duckdb` dependency in `package.json` to a release whose node-pre-gyp closure resolves `tar@>=7.5.19`, then `pnpm install`; or\n2. `pnpm.overrides: { \"tar@<7.5.19\": \"^7.5.19\" }` in `package.json` to force the transitive resolution.\n3. Commit lockfile, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`. One bump to ≥7.5.21 also clears the sibling tar CVEs (59874/59871/59875) filed separately.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "tar",
                "installed_version": "7.5.13",
                "package_ecosystem": "npm",
                "manifest_path": "pnpm-lock.yaml",
                "fixed_version": "7.5.19",
                "introduced_by": "duckdb@1.4.4",
                "dependency_path": "duckdb@1.4.4 > @mapbox/node-pre-gyp@2.0.3 > tar@7.5.13",
                "reachability": "imported",
                "reachability_evidence": "No application code imports `tar` directly (`rg -n \"require\\(['\\\"]tar['\\\"]|from ['\\\"]tar['\\\"]\"` over `--type ts` on src/ returned no hits). It is reached only through `duckdb`'s `@mapbox/node-pre-gyp` install/extract step. `duckdb` itself IS imported by application code at src/services/furnaceSqlService.ts:55 (`require('duckdb').Database`) and src/services/duckdb/pool.ts:49. Affected-symbol (`tar.x/tar.t`) check inside node-pre-gyp was not performed."
              }
            }
          }
        },
