          "ruleId": "CWE-436",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-53655 in tar 7.5.13 via duckdb (file smuggling via inconsistent PAX/ GNU long-name parsing)\n\nThe transitive package **`tar@7.5.13`** (via `duckdb`'s `@mapbox/node-pre-gyp`) is affected by CVE-2026-53655: node-tar applies a PAX extended header's `size=` record (and other PAX overrides) to the next header entry of ANY type, including intermediary metadata headers such as GNU long-name (`L`) or long-link (`K`) entries. Per POSIX pax, a PAX header describes the next FILE entry, not the intermediary extension headers — so a specifically-crafted archive can smuggle file content past archive-scanning or produce inconsistent extraction. Fixed in `7.5.16`. This is an integrity (file-smuggling) issue, not just DoS."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
