              "cve": "CVE-2026-53655",
              "cwe": "CWE-436",
              "impact": "An attacker-supplied tar archive can have a file's contents silently attributed to the wrong entry / extracted under a smuggled name, letting crafted content slip past archive-inspection or integrity checks. Local extraction with a victim needing to consume the archive (UI:R), confidentiality low + integrity high.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** node-tar < 7.5.16 applies PAX `size=`/overrides to the next header of any type (including GNU `L`/`K` intermediary headers) instead of only the next file entry, producing parser-differential \"file smuggling\". **Chain:** `duckdb@1.4.4 > @mapbox/node-pre-gyp@2.0.3 > tar@7.5.13`. **Trivy:** Severity=MEDIUM, CVSS redhat:6.1 (CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N), CWE-436.",
