              "target": "/workspace/tellus",
              "cve": "CVE-2026-12590",
              "cwe": "CWE-770",
              "impact": "Oversized request bodies are accepted when the `limit` option is misconfigured to an invalid value, allowing memory-exhaustion DoS. Requires the (high-complexity) precondition of a misconfigured limit; availability impact.",
              "technical_analysis": "**Root cause:** invalid `limit` (NaN/garbage) makes `bytes.parse` return null, skipping the body-size guard. **Chain:** `express@4.22.1 > body-parser@1.20.4` (express is the direct dep; this app is an Express server). **Trivy:** Severity=LOW, CVSS nvd:5.9 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H), CWE-770.",
              "remediation_steps": "Fix at the direct level: bump `express` in `package.json` to a release whose closure resolves `body-parser@>=1.20.6` (express 4.19+ / 5.x line), or `pnpm.overrides: { \"body-parser@<1.20.6\": \"^1.20.6\" }`. Regenerate lockfile, verify with `trivy fs pnpm-lock.yaml`.",
              "dependency_metadata": {
                "package_name": "body-parser",
                "installed_version": "1.20.4",
