        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-269",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "BFLA: zero-role remote users manage superadmin function-publish grants and self-escalate to function-publish code execution (CODE_REPOS_TEST_AUTH dev fallback reachable behind proxy)\n\nThe function-publish admin surface (`/api/v1/functions/admin/*`) is protected by `requireSuperadmin`, but the upstream authentication middleware fabricates a superadmin principal for any request that appears to come from localhost. Because the deployment sits behind a gateway/proxy, `req.socket.remoteAddress` is loopback for all callers, so any authenticated remote user — even one with zero platform roles — can list, create, and revoke function-publish grants. A zero-role user can therefore grant itself a global function-publish grant and reach arbitrary TypeScript function-publish code execution (Broken Function-Level Authorization → privilege escalation → RCE)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/services/codeRepos/middleware/principal.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 80,
                  "endLine": 81,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const DEV_FALLBACK_PRINCIPAL =\n  \"53cf9bcf-4c20-4aed-83f4-3c7e405453b4/OWNER,EDITOR,READER,tellus-superadmin\";"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Fabricated superadmin dev principal (informational)"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/services/codeRepos/middleware/principal.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 187,
                  "endLine": 191
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Fail-closed: reject when no test principal instead of fabricating superadmin"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/services/functions/admin/routes.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 431,
                  "endLine": 434,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "router.get(\n    \"/function-publish-grants\",\n    asyncRoute(async (req: Request, res: Response) => {\n      if (!requireSuperadmin(req, res)) return;"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Superadmin-gated grants list (authz check is present and correct)"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/v1/functions/admin/function-publish-grants",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/services/codeRepos/middleware/principal.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 187,
                        "endLine": 191
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "// Never fabricate a superadmin principal. When the test-auth flag is on\n      // and no explicit X-Tellus-Test-Principal header is supplied, reject.\n      // (The prior localhost dev fallback granted tellus-superadmin to any\n      // caller whose socket appeared loopback — trivially reached behind a\n      // proxy/gateway, yielding a full privilege-escalation / grant-management\n      // bypass. Removed: fail-closed.)\n      sendUnauthenticated(res, req, \"Test principal header required\");\n      return;"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "1. Remove `DEV_FALLBACK_PRINCIPAL` entirely — never fabricate a superadmin principal.\n2. When the test-auth flag is on and no `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header is present, reject with 401 instead of falling back to a privileged identity.\n3. Strengthen `isLocalhost`: additionally require `X-Forwarded-For` to be absent or loopback and require `NODE_ENV===\"development\"` explicitly; never honor the fallback for a request that presents a real JWT for a different user.\n4. Add boot-time fail-fast when `CODE_REPOS_TEST_AUTH=1` and the app listens on a non-loopback interface or sits behind a proxy (detect via an env such as `TELLUS_BEHIND_PROXY`).\n5. Add a regression test asserting that a remote zero-role JWT with no test headers receives 403 on all `/api/v1/functions/admin/*` methods.",
                "markdown": "1. Remove `DEV_FALLBACK_PRINCIPAL` entirely — never fabricate a superadmin principal.\n2. When the test-auth flag is on and no `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header is present, reject with 401 instead of falling back to a privileged identity.\n3. Strengthen `isLocalhost`: additionally require `X-Forwarded-For` to be absent or loopback and require `NODE_ENV===\"development\"` explicitly; never honor the fallback for a request that presents a real JWT for a different user.\n4. Add boot-time fail-fast when `CODE_REPOS_TEST_AUTH=1` and the app listens on a non-loopback interface or sits behind a proxy (detect via an env such as `TELLUS_BEHIND_PROXY`).\n5. Add a regression test asserting that a remote zero-role JWT with no test headers receives 403 on all `/api/v1/functions/admin/*` methods."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "43a8d9ea118a71f2bdefcfd594fd1e2ca01dd8352ccfc4abb049e671925b92b6"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "8.8",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "76f0320d419eb42f0a0edf303392e0bdc2a92cc6118ed047c3ed271e7c8ee77c",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0024",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 8.8,
              "timestamp": "2026-08-18 06:43:55 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:3000",
              "endpoint": "/api/v1/functions/admin/function-publish-grants",
              "method": "POST",
              "cwe": "CWE-269",
              "impact": "Any holder of a valid JWT for any user can manage superadmin-only publish grants: list all grants and the publish audit log, create arbitrary grants, and revoke other principals' grants. By creating a `global` grant bound to its own `keycloak_sub`, a zero-role user satisfies `authorizePublish()` in `services/functions/executionPolicy.ts` (~lines 368-374) and can then publish and execute arbitrary TypeScript functions through the worker_threads+vm executor pool (`src/services/functionExecutor.ts`, documented as not a security boundary). This is a full self-driven privilege escalation from a plain authenticated user to remote code execution, plus the ability to disrupt others by revoking their grants (Availability). Confirmed up to an active global grant; the publish step itself was not executed.",
              "technical_analysis": "Mount chain: `server.ts:1044` mounts `app.use(\"/api/v1/functions/admin\", createFunctionPublishAdminRouter({ pool }))`; the router applies `router.use(requireCodeReposAuth())` at `services/functions/admin/routes.ts:194`, and each handler (`routes.ts:81-92`, the GET list at `routes.ts:431-434`, plus `:209`/`:565`) correctly calls `requireSuperadmin(req, res)`. The authorization check itself is present — the failure is in the principal that reaches it.\n\n`src/services/codeRepos/middleware/principal.ts` `requireCodeReposAuth()`: when `isTestAuthBypassEnabled(\"CODE_REPOS_TEST_AUTH\")` is true and NO `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header is present, it falls to the \"localhost dev fallback\" (lines ~166-191). `isLocalhost(req)` (line ~69) checks only `req.socket.remoteAddress ∈ {127.0.0.1, ::1, ::ffff:127.0.0.1}`. Behind the deployment's gateway/proxy, the app sees a loopback-ish peer for every caller, so remote users satisfy it and are handed `DEV_FALLBACK_PRINCIPAL = \"53cf9bcf-4c20-4aed-83f4-3c7e405453b4/OWNER,EDITOR,READER,tellus-superadmin\"` (lines 80-81) — the admin's real Keycloak `sub` plus `tellus-superadmin` — without presenting any credential beyond an arbitrary valid Keycloak JWT. `requireSuperadmin` then sees `tellus-superadmin` and passes.\n\nConfig: `.env:137` sets `CODE_REPOS_TEST_AUTH=1`; `docker-compose.override.yml:33` defaults it to 0 but `.env` is the loaded value; `utils/testAuthGate.ts` only fails closed when `NODE_ENV===\"production\"`, and the running app has `NODE_ENV=development`. The whole bypass chain is therefore ACTIVE in this deployment and in any environment with `CODE_REPOS_TEST_AUTH=1` + non-production `NODE_ENV` + a localhost-appearing proxy.\n\nAttacker verified: `cypress-nogroups@tellus.local` (`sub bcd2551e-b985-4d6f-97ff-e0e087a87e20`, realm roles only `offline_access` + `default-roles-tellus`, zero platform roles), no `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header sent. Contrast: repeating the request with a crafted `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` carrying `roles:[]` returns HTTP 403 `Functions:PermissionDenied superadmin-required` — proving `requireSuperadmin` works and that the bypass comes from the fabricated-principal fallback, not a missing check.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Remove `DEV_FALLBACK_PRINCIPAL` entirely — never fabricate a superadmin principal.\n2. When the test-auth flag is on and no `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header is present, reject with 401 instead of falling back to a privileged identity.\n3. Strengthen `isLocalhost`: additionally require `X-Forwarded-For` to be absent or loopback and require `NODE_ENV===\"development\"` explicitly; never honor the fallback for a request that presents a real JWT for a different user.\n4. Add boot-time fail-fast when `CODE_REPOS_TEST_AUTH=1` and the app listens on a non-loopback interface or sits behind a proxy (detect via an env such as `TELLUS_BEHIND_PROXY`).\n5. Add a regression test asserting that a remote zero-role JWT with no test headers receives 403 on all `/api/v1/functions/admin/*` methods.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Mint a bearer token for the zero-role attacker (`cypress-nogroups@tellus.local`) from Keycloak (realm `tellus`, client `tellus-frontend`). Send no `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header.\n2. `GET /api/v1/functions/admin/function-publish-grants` → HTTP 200 returning the full grant list (a superadmin-only endpoint per the code). `GET .../function-publish-audit-log` → HTTP 200 with publish events.\n3. `POST /api/v1/functions/admin/function-publish-grants` with body `{\"subjectType\":\"keycloak_sub\",\"subjectId\":\"<attacker_sub>\",\"scopeType\":\"global\",\"reason\":\"idor-agent-privesc-test\"}` → HTTP 201; the created grant is `status: active` and `grantedBy` shows the fabricated principal `53cf9bcf-4c20-4aed-83f4-3c7e405453b4`.\n4. `GET /api/v1/functions/admin/function-publish-grants` again → confirms the attacker-bound global grant is now active (this is the row `authorizePublish()` matches to permit publish → code execution).\n5. `DELETE /api/v1/functions/admin/function-publish-grants/{existing_grant_id}` → HTTP 200, revoking another principal's grant (re-created afterwards to leave the environment clean).\n6. Contrast: repeat step 3 with a crafted `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header carrying empty roles → HTTP 403 `Functions:PermissionDenied superadmin-required`, proving the check works and the bypass is the dev fallback.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-835",
          "ruleIndex": 17,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-59877 in protobufjs 7.6.2 via @opentelemetry/sdk-node (DoS — infinite loop on crafted .proto schema)\n\nThe transitive package **`protobufjs@7.6.2`** (pinned via `pnpm-lock.yaml` through `@opentelemetry/sdk-node` → `@grpc/proto-loader`) is affected by CVE-2026-59877: option names are parsed by advancing through schema tokens until an `=` token is reached without checking for end of input, so a crafted `.proto` schema that opens an option declaration and ends prematurely makes `Root.load`/`Root.loadSync` loop indefinitely. Fixed in `7.6.5` / `8.6.6`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
