        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-79",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored XSS / Active Content via Attachment Upload (inline content-disposition, cross-user readable)\n\nThe v2 attachment upload endpoint accepts user-supplied files with arbitrary filenames and MIME types, stores them verbatim, and the content endpoint serves them back with `Content-Disposition: inline` and the stored `Content-Type`. An authenticated low-privilege user can upload `text/html` or `image/svg+xml` content that any other authenticated user's browser renders in-line when fetched. Cross-user read succeeds (viewer's attachment is served to an admin), and although CSP blocks inline JavaScript, active content is still rendered, enabling phishing UI and CSS-based exfiltration of DOM data."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/routes/v2/attachmentsV2.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 80,
