                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "// Code Repositories must always pass through real authentication.\n  // Do not allowlist this prefix; requireCodeReposAuth (production path)\n  // must validate JWT/PAT for every sub-route, including functions/invoke."
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "1. Require real authentication for every code-repositories sub-route: remove the `/api/v1/code-repositories` global allowlist entry in `globalAuth.ts` and delete the dev \"fallback principal\" substitution in `requireCodeReposAuth` so no unauthenticated request is ever granted an always-authorized synthetic identity. Restrict test-mode principal synthesis to an explicit `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header under `isTestAuthBypassEnabled`, and never give the synthesized principal publish-capable roles.\n2. Gate working-tree / `inlineSource` execution behind the same `authorizePublish()` boundary used by the registry publish endpoints, so server-side code execution requires explicit authorization (the executor is documented as NOT an untrusted-code sandbox).\n3. As defense-in-depth, add a sandbox guard that rejects constructor-chain escapes (`globalThis.constructor.constructor`, the `Function` constructor) for untrusted sources, and move inline execution exclusively into the worker-pool / locked-down subprocess.\n4. Extend the production boot assertion (`assertNoTestAuthInProduction`) with a check that no route admits anonymous code execution, so the dev toggles can never silently reach production.",
                "markdown": "1. Require real authentication for every code-repositories sub-route: remove the `/api/v1/code-repositories` global allowlist entry in `globalAuth.ts` and delete the dev \"fallback principal\" substitution in `requireCodeReposAuth` so no unauthenticated request is ever granted an always-authorized synthetic identity. Restrict test-mode principal synthesis to an explicit `X-Tellus-Test-Principal` header under `isTestAuthBypassEnabled`, and never give the synthesized principal publish-capable roles.\n2. Gate working-tree / `inlineSource` execution behind the same `authorizePublish()` boundary used by the registry publish endpoints, so server-side code execution requires explicit authorization (the executor is documented as NOT an untrusted-code sandbox).\n3. As defense-in-depth, add a sandbox guard that rejects constructor-chain escapes (`globalThis.constructor.constructor`, the `Function` constructor) for untrusted sources, and move inline execution exclusively into the worker-pool / locked-down subprocess.\n4. Extend the production boot assertion (`assertNoTestAuthInProduction`) with a check that no route admits anonymous code execution, so the dev toggles can never silently reach production."
              }
